marily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1591887286", "reactions": [{"reaction_type": 3, "count": 8}, {"reaction_type": 5, "count": 6}, {"reaction_type": 11, "count": 1}, {"reaction_type": 1, "count": 1}, {"reaction_type": 2, "count": 1}, {"reaction_type": 4, "count": 1}]}, {"recommendationid": "74578127", "author": {"steamid": "76561198141927391", "personaname": "Jacket", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198141927391/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 6, "playtime_forever": 6547, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 5346, "last_played": 1617729147, "avatar": "4f570497f69258a4c87a8094f20594402ddda138"}, "language": "english", "review": "A good game on its own, but mixed in with some mods (ALOT,EGM,MEHEM) this has to be the best game in the trilogy, shame you have to download origin cause that client sucks major a**. \n\nAnother thing I recommend buying every dlc, I'm against giving EA money but the dlc for this game is in my opinion worth every penny. Omega is great if you like the character of Aria, otherwise it's your typical shooter. Leviathan adds some lore to the story and a little bit of Lovecraft is always welcomed. Citadel dlc is the epitome of fan service, it's cheesy and corny in all the right way, it adds a little humor in ME3's rather dark tone and is the main reason why buying the dlc pack is so damn worth it", "timestamp_created": 1597866350, "timestamp_updated": 1597866350, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 2, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.502451300621032715", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1591887286", "reactions": []}]}